@startuml

title Alcohol Concentration Test - Class Diagram

class Person {
    - name: str
    - gender: str
    - mass: float

    + __init__(
        name: str,
        gender: str,
        mass: float
    ): None

    + distribution_factor(): float
    + __str__(): str
}

class AlcoholTest {
    - test_name: str
    - limit: float

    + __init__(
        test_name: str,
        limit: float = 0.5
    ): None

    + alcohol_amount(
        volume: float,
        alcohol_content: float,
        density: float = 0.8
    ): float

    + concentration(
        person: Person,
        volume: float,
        alcohol_content: float,
        density: float = 0.8
    ): float

    + passed(
        person: Person,
        volume: float,
        alcohol_content: float,
        density: float = 0.8
    ): bool
}

class Main {
    + main(): None
}

class TestPerson {
    + test_create_male_person(): None
    + test_create_female_person(): None
    + test_invalid_gender(): None
    + test_invalid_mass(): None
}

class TestAlcoholTest {
    + setUp(): None
    + test_alcohol_amount(): None
    + test_hansel_passes(): None
    + test_gretel_does_not_pass(): None
}

Main ..> Person : creates
Main ..> AlcoholTest : uses

TestPerson ..> Person : tests
TestAlcoholTest ..> Person : tests
TestAlcoholTest ..> AlcoholTest : tests

note right of AlcoholTest
Widmark formula:

A = V * alcohol_content * density

c = A / (mass * r)

A: alcohol amount in grams
V: drink volume in milliliters
r: distribution factor
c: concentration in g/kg
end note

note bottom of Person
Male distribution factor: 0.7
Female distribution factor: 0.6
end note

@enduml
